{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791803993,"nonce":"aSWWVADPl9x86EFJ0B6qH9ZiyTc=","title":"Tooltip does not open when its child button receives keyboard focus","message":"The editor uses the built-in Tooltip around built-in Button controls. Calling Focus.set(button, true) correctly focuses the button but creates zero .ui-tooltip nodes; the hover path opens normally.\n\nFocused reproducer: chimpmonk/repro/ashui_tooltip_focus/Repro.hx. Build with AshUI haxe and components/haxe, hlwindow and hlwgpu Haxe classpaths, tink_hxx and hashlink, --macro ashui.ui.Markup.enable(), then run the .hl beside blinc_abi.hdll. The current native build prints “Keyboard-focused button: 0 tooltip nodes” and fails the one-tooltip assertion.\n\nTooltip.render listens for focus on its wrapper Interaction and checks that wrapper’s focusVisible. Focus.set fires the focus event on the actual button; that event does not bubble to the wrapper. focusWithin is updated on ancestors. Expected: a keyboard-focused descendant opens its tooltip immediately, leaves it visible while keyboard focus stays within, and closes on leaving the trigger. Preserve existing pointer-delay and top-layer exit behaviour.","files":null}]}